<title>POLAND: Merrill maintains Export as &quot;accumulate&quot;.</title>
<headline>Merrill maintains Export as &quot;accumulate&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch in London maintained its accumulate rating for Polish construction firm Mostostal Export SA accumulate rating, expecting its 20-percent real earnings per share growth in 1997.</p>
<p>It said in a report dated March 14 it expected Mostostal's P/E ratio to fall to 8.8 in 1997 from last year's 12 as it saw its EPS rising to 0.96 zlotys from 0.7 last year.</p>
<p>&quot;With construction activities accelerating, we expect 20 percent real EPS growth this year placing the stocks on a PE (97E) of 8.8x which is 54 percent of the prospective Polish market PE,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
